als International Co., Cambridge, MA, USA."}]}}, {"fullName": "Madabhushi A", "lastName": "Madabhushi", "firstName": "Anant", "initials": "A", "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "Case Western Reserve University, Cleveland, OH, USA."}, {"affiliation": "Louis Stokes Cleveland Veterans Affair Medical Center, Cleveland, OH, USA."}]}}, {"fullName": "Shah P", "lastName": "Shah", "firstName": "Parantu", "initials": "P", "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "EMD Serono R&D Institute, Billerica, MA, USA."}]}}, {"fullName": "Spitzer M", "lastName": "Spitzer", "firstName": "Michaela", "initials": "M", "authorId": {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0003-1967-3726"}, "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "Open Targets and European Molecular Biology Laboratory, European Bioinformatics Institute, Cambridge, UK.", "affiliationOrgId": "ror.org/02catss52"}]}}, {"fullName": "Zhao S", "lastName": "Zhao", "firstName": "Shanrong", "initials": "S", "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "Pfizer Worldwide Research and Development, Cambridge, MA, USA."}]}}]}, "authorIdList": {"authorId": [{"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-2227-8834"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-7390-8795"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0003-1967-3726"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0003-2016-9754"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0003-2092-2486"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0003-2525-5598"}]}, "dataLinksTagsList": {"dataLinkstag": ["altmetrics", "supporting_data"]}, "journalInfo": {"issue": "6", "volume": "18", "journalIssueId": 2822973, "dateOfPublication": "2019 Jun", "monthOfPublication": 6, "yearOfPublication": 2019, "journal": {"medlineAbbreviation": "Nat Rev Drug Discov", "title": "Nature reviews. Drug discovery", "essn": "1474-1784", "issn": "1474-1776", "isoabbreviation": "Nat Rev Drug Discov", "nlmid": "101124171"}, "printPublicationDate": "2019-06-01"}, "pubYear": "2019", "pageInfo": "463-477", "abstractText": "Drug discovery and development pipelines are long, complex and depend on numerous factors. Machine learning (ML) approaches provide a set of tools that can improve discovery and decision making for well-specified questions with abundant, high-quality data. Opportunities to apply ML occur in all stages of drug discovery. Examples include target validation, identification of prognostic biomarkers and analysis of digital pathology data in clinical trials. Applications have ranged in context and methodology, with some approaches yielding accurate predictions and insights. The challenges of applying ML lie primarily with the lack of interpretability and repeatability of ML-generated results, which may limit their application. In all areas, systematic and comprehensive high-dimensional data still need to be generated. With ongoing efforts to tackle these issues, as well as increasing awareness of the factors needed to validate ML approaches, the application of ML can promote data-driven decision making and has the potential to speed up the process and reduce failure rates in drug discovery and development.", "affiliation": "European Molecular Biology Laboratory, European Bioinformatics Institute, Cambridge, UK. jessicav@ebi.ac.uk.", "publicationStatus": "ppublish", "language": "eng", "pubModel": "Print", "pubTypeList": {"pubType": ["research-article", "Review", "Journal Article"]}, "grantsList": {"grant": [{"agency": "NCI NIH HHS", "acronym": "CA", "grantId": "R01 CA216579", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "NCI NIH HHS", "acronym": "CA", "grantId": "U24 CA199374", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "NCI NIH HHS", "acronym": "CA", "grantId": "R01 CA202752", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "NCI NIH HHS", "acronym": "CA", "grantId": "R01 CA220581", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "BLRD VA", "acronym": "BX", "grantId": "I01 BX004121", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "NCI NIH HHS", "acronym": "CA", "grantId": "R01 CA208236", "orderIn": 0}]}, "meshHea